    "question": {
      ":question/id": "af45c5c3-91a1-5607-bf89-9cfa7beab691",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $y=10x+8?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nThe line $y=10x+8$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $10.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=-\\frac{1}{10}x-9$ has a slope of $-\\frac{1}{10}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n10\\cdot -\\frac{1}{10}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=-\\frac{1}{10}x-9$ is perpendicular to the given line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "85e7701d-aafb-5911-9003-d9d462d822a6",
